<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24039" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-sufflo</span></b> , āvi, ātum,
		1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to blow</i> or <i>breathe into</i> or
				<i>upon</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insufflavit in faciem ejus flatum vitae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Res. Carn. 5</span></i>
			; Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ στεφ.</span> 10, 9, 19: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per fistulam os plenum vino,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. 2, 21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ei spiritum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Sap. 15, 11</span></i>
			. — <b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Johan. 20, 22</span></i>.</div>
